{
  "comment": "The official documents HttpAsm is built from, pinned by SHA-256. Each file is the RFC Editor's canonical copy: the published XML (RFCXML v3, whose pn attributes number every paragraph) for RFCs from 2019 on, the text file for older ones. specs.cs fetch downloads them into rfc/ and checks the hashes; specs.cs extract turns them into requirements.tsv. The one ITU-T Recommendation (format itu: X.690, the encoding rules) is the ITU's PDF, free to download but not to redistribute: fetch downloads it into itu/ (ignored by git) and checks its hash, and its rows are transcribed by hand, clause by clause, in x690.tsv, which extract reads instead. milestone: the docs/DESIGN.md milestone that implements the document (open: not decided yet).",
